1
00:00:02,872 --> 00:00:04,532
(Amy:)There was water everywhere.

2
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:05,900
(Amy:)It was such a mess.

3
00:00:05,965 --> 00:00:07,915
(Leonard:)That stinks. How long are you
out of the apartment?

4
00:00:07,919 --> 00:00:08,919
(Amy:)About five weeks.

5
00:00:08,987 --> 00:00:10,227
Ugh! Did you lose
anything valuable?

6
00:00:10,255 --> 00:00:11,725
(Amy:)Well, the pipe was
over my closet,

7
00:00:11,790 --> 00:00:13,190
(Amy:)so all my
clothes are gone.

8
00:00:13,258 --> 00:00:15,698
(Penny:)Oh, so nothing. Great.

9
00:00:16,464 --> 00:00:18,174
(Penny:)Do they know why
the pipe burst?

10
00:00:18,235 --> 00:00:19,435
(Amy:)They didn't say.

11
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:20,933
(Leonard:)Buildings
that have a combination

12
00:00:21,004 --> 00:00:22,204
(Leonard:)of copper and galvanized steel

13
00:00:22,272 --> 00:00:24,932
(Leonard:)are susceptible to
pinholes and corrosion

14
00:00:25,036 --> 00:00:27,376
(Leonard:)caused by the mobility
of ions in the water.

15
00:00:31,267 --> 00:00:34,137
(Leonard:)Can't have your head shoved
in a toilet as much as I did

16
00:00:34,137 --> 00:00:37,937
(Leonard:)and not pick up a few things
about plumbing.

17
00:00:38,008 --> 00:00:41,208
(Penny:)Well, if you need a place to
crash, you can stay with us.

18
00:00:41,278 --> 00:00:42,748
- Really?
- Of course.

19
00:00:42,813 --> 00:00:45,683
(Penny:)You can stay in Leonard's room,
and we'll stay at my place.

20
00:00:45,749 --> 00:00:47,349
(Amy:)You're sure
that's not an inconvenience?

21
00:00:47,417 --> 00:00:48,687
(Penny:)No, not at all.

22
00:00:48,752 --> 00:00:50,052
(Leonard:)And we live with Sheldon,

23
00:00:50,120 --> 00:00:52,420
so the word "inconvenience"
has really lost all meaning.

24
00:00:53,857 --> 00:00:57,397
(Amy:)So, technically, I'd be
moving in with my boyfriend?

25
00:00:57,461 --> 00:00:58,931
(Penny:)I guess so.

26
00:00:58,995 --> 00:01:01,445
(Penny:)I'd finally get to live
alone with my husband.

27
00:01:01,921 --> 00:01:04,081
(Amy:)Oh, my, this is
a big step.

28
00:01:04,084 --> 00:01:04,834
(Leonard:)Mm-hmm.

29
00:01:04,832 --> 00:01:06,832
(Leonard:)For two of us, it's in
the right direction.

30
00:01:12,005 --> 00:01:15,875
(Sheldon:)Why are you all smiling
like crazy people?

31
00:01:15,942 --> 00:01:19,382
♪ Our whole universe
was in a hot, dense state ♪

